     1	"""ProviderLedgerOracle (HARN-1a / HARN-2) — enforces the soak provider constraint
     2	over the provider-call-ledger evidence.
     3	
     4	Zero-opinion: it reads the ledger (the list of provider calls made during the run)
     5	and the scenario's provider assertion, and fails on a concrete, observed violation:
     6	- a call to a FORBIDDEN host (default: openrouter) or a host that isn't the required one
     7	  → PROVIDER_FORBIDDEN
     8	- a call using the WRONG model (not the pinned soak model) → PROVIDER_WRONG_MODEL
     9	- a call that fired AFTER the conversation went terminal (runaway burn)
    10	  → PROVIDER_CALL_AFTER_TERMINAL
    11	
    12	Enforcement is OPT-IN per scenario: it runs only when the scenario declares
    13	``assertions.provider`` (so ordinary dev scenarios are not failed for using other
    14	providers). When enforcement is required but no ledger was captured, it SKIPS with a
    15	reason rather than passing or failing — absent evidence is not a verdict. (The final
    16	P17 soak requires the ledger present + enforcement on.)
    17	
    18	scenario.assertions.provider (all keys optional):
    19	    {"forbid_host_substr": ["openrouter"],   # default ["openrouter"] if provider asserted
    20	     "require_host_substr": "minimax",        # every call's host must contain this
